# English (US, international, with dead keys): Microsoft's "United States-International".
# The apostrophe, quotation mark, grave accent, tilde and Shift+6 are dead keys: they type
# nothing until the next key, which they put an accent on (a space types the accent itself).
# AltGr types the accented letters and the symbols of that layout. Good for Afrikaans.
title "English (US, international, with dead keys)"
altgr

# The number row.
key GRAVE dead:grave dead:tilde
key 1 1 ! ¡ ¹
key 2 2 @ ²
key 3 3 # ³
key 4 4 $ ¤ £
key 5 5 % €
key 6 6 dead:circumflex ¼
key 7 7 & ½
key 8 8 * ¾
key 9 9 ( ‘
key 0 0 ) ’
key MINUS - _ ¥
key EQUALS = + × ÷

# The top letter row.
key Q q Q ä Ä
key W w W å Å
key E e E é É
key R r R ®
key T t T þ Þ
key Y y Y ü Ü
key U u U ú Ú
key I i I í Í
key O o O ó Ó
key P p P ö Ö
key LEFT_BRACKET [ { «
key RIGHT_BRACKET ] } »
key BACKSLASH \ | ¬ ¦

# The home row.
key A a A á Á
key S s S ß §
key D d D ð Ð
key F f F
key G g G
key H h H
key J j J
key K k K
key L l L ø Ø
key SEMICOLON ; : ¶ °
key APOSTROPHE dead:acute dead:diaeresis ´ ¨

# The bottom row. The key beside the left Shift, which US keyboards mostly lack, types what
# US keyboards that have it type.
key 102ND \ |
key Z z Z æ Æ
key X x X
key C c C © ¢
key V v V
key B b B
key N n N ñ Ñ
key M m M µ
key COMMA , < ç Ç
key PERIOD . >
key SLASH / ? ¿

# The space bar.
key SPACE space

# What each dead key does to the letter after it.
dead acute a á A Á e é E É i í I Í o ó O Ó u ú U Ú y ý Y Ý c ç C Ç space '
dead grave a à A À e è E È i ì I Ì o ò O Ò u ù U Ù space `
dead circumflex a â A Â e ê E Ê i î I Î o ô O Ô u û U Û space ^
dead diaeresis a ä A Ä e ë E Ë i ï I Ï o ö O Ö u ü U Ü y ÿ Y Ÿ space "
dead tilde a ã A Ã n ñ N Ñ o õ O Õ space ~

# The keypad (digits only while Num Lock is on).
key KP_DIVIDE / /
key KP_MULTIPLY * *
key KP_MINUS - -
key KP_7 7 7
key KP_8 8 8
key KP_9 9 9
key KP_PLUS + +
key KP_4 4 4
key KP_5 5 5
key KP_6 6 6
key KP_1 1 1
key KP_2 2 2
key KP_3 3 3
key KP_0 0 0
key KP_PERIOD . .

